From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Johannes Schrimpf <johannes.schrimpf@blueye.no>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 10:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] PCI: tegra194: Set the core clock for the actual link speed

tegra_pcie_icc_set() sets the core clock to pcie_gen_freq[speed - 1], but since
mainline commit 205b3d02d57c ("PCI: tegra194: Fix possible array out of bounds
access") the table has a placeholder at index 0.

Commit 91cedff9cb44 ("NVIDIA: SAUCE: PCI: tegra194: Add core monitor clock
support"), authored before commit 205b3d02d57c but applied after it, changed
the mainline pcie_gen_freq[speed] back to speed - 1, so the clock is one PCIe
generation too low: 125 MHz instead of 250 MHz on Gen3, 250 MHz instead of
500 MHz on Gen4.

Use pcie_gen_freq[speed] as mainline does.

Fixes: 91cedff9cb44 ("NVIDIA: SAUCE: PCI: tegra194: Add core monitor clock support")
Upstream-Status: Pending
Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Johannes Schrimpf <johannes.schrimpf@blueye.no>
---
The bug was found with Claude Opus 5.5 in Claude Code, which also wrote
this fix.

Tested on an Orin NX with a Gen3 x4 NVMe: the core clock is 250 MHz with
the fix, 125 MHz without.

 drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-tegra194.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-tegra194.c b/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-tegra194.c
index 4070105..03b6e69 100644
--- a/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-tegra194.c
+++ b/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-tegra194.c
@@ -473,7 +473,7 @@ static void tegra_pcie_icc_set(struct tegra_pcie_dw *pcie)
 		speed = 0;
 
 	if ((speed > 0) && (speed <= 4) && !pcie->is_safety_platform)
-		clk_set_rate(pcie->core_clk, pcie_gen_freq[speed - 1]);
+		clk_set_rate(pcie->core_clk, pcie_gen_freq[speed]);
 }
 
 static void apply_bad_link_workaround(struct dw_pcie_rp *pp)
